.TH COMMAND * 2014-04-08 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBdb.traceOff()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
traceOff - Close the tracing function of the database engine, and
then export the information in to binary files.
/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump
.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp 2

.sp 2

.sp 2
traceOff(\fB<dumpFile>\fR)

.SH "CATEGORY"

.sp 2

.sp 2
Sdb
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
Turn off the database engine program tracking and export tracking results to
binary files.

.SH "PARAMETERS"
.sp 2
\fBDump file (string)\fR
.br
       Name of dump file.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.sp 2
On success, return void.
.sp 2
On error, exception will be thrown.
.sp 2
.SH "ERRORS"
.sp 2
when exception happen, use getLastError() to get the error code and use
getLastErrMsg() to get error message.
For more detial, please reference to Troubleshooting.

.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
Turn off the database engine program tracking and export tracking results to
binary files, /opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceOff( "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump" )
.sp 2
Using traceFmt() to analysis the binary file.
.sp 2
>\ traceFmt(\ 0,\ "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump",\ "/opt/sequoiadb/trace_output"\ )
.sp 2